# The committer's harness.
#
# It writes the commit message. It does not commit — it cannot, having no shell
# and no git. The orchestrator takes the message and runs the commit itself.
#
# That split is deliberate. Writing a sentence about a change is a job for a
# model; deciding that a repository gets written to is not, and a station with
# `bash` on a real working tree is a much larger thing to trust than a station
# that returns a paragraph.
TOOLS="read,grep,find,ls"
MODEL="anthropic/claude-opus-4-7"
EXTENSION=""
